!panic: fixedbugs2702agetcontextandsetcontextpairthehandlercallsitafterthecoroutineswapsbackontheownstackisrefused.answer was called while a signal handler of C's that this runtime saw begin had switched to another context (`swapcontext`, or `setcontext` into a context `makecontext` made) and had not been seen to switch back or to end: either C called it on that other context, or C abandoned the handler by a switch this runtime cannot tell from one that comes back. A handler not seen to end is held to be running, where neither this runtime's memory nor the C library's is safe to use. No function of the program is a signal handler: after `hero_net_catch_stop() -> i64` (`hero_net.h`), Ctrl-C, SIGTERM and `hero_net_ask_stop() -> ()` only make `hero_net_stop_asked() -> i64` answer 1 and a waiting call of that layer answer stopped; `hero_signal_watch(sig: i32) -> i64` (`hero_os.h`) counts any other signal, and `hero_signal_take(sig: i32) -> i64` gives the count since its last call
